  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 602.10 Coastal flood risk",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 602.10 “Coastal flood risk” means the likelihood and adverse consequences of flooding from seawater and is a function of the coastal flood hazard at a location and the exposure and vulnerability of people and their assets to that hazard.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
